        ["During abdominal soft-tissue work, a client reports tenderness in the right upper quadrant that radiates to the right scapula, and it gets worse after fatty meals. Which organ is most likely involved?", ["Gallbladder", "Appendix", "Spleen", "Urinary bladder"], "The gallbladder is in the RUQ and can refer pain to the right shoulder or scapula, especially after fatty meals. Stop the treatment and refer the client for medical evaluation."],
        ["Turning the sole of the foot outward, away from the midline, is called:", ["Eversion", "Inversion", "Dorsiflexion", "Supination of the forearm"], "Eversion turns the sole outward and inversion turns it inward. An inversion mechanism is the classic lateral ankle sprain."],
        ["A coworker asks how the hands are positioned in anatomical position. Which answer is correct?", ["Palms face forward", "Palms face backward", "Palms face the thighs", "Palms face downward"], "In anatomical position the forearms are supinated and the palms face forward. This is why the thumb is lateral in standard descriptions."],
        ["A note for a patient with a right L5 radiculopathy says 'pain radiates to the ipsilateral buttock and lateral leg.' Which side is symptomatic?", ["Right", "Left", "Both", "It cannot be determined"], "Ipsilateral means the same side as the reference point, here the right-sided radiculopathy. Contralateral would have meant the left side."],
        ["A wound is described as being on the 'volar' surface of the wrist. Where is it?", ["On the palm side", "On the back of the wrist", "On the thumb side", "On the little-finger side"], "Volar is synonymous with palmar, the palm side of the hand and wrist. The back of the wrist is dorsal, the thumb side is radial, and the little-finger side is ulnar."],
        ["A patient with heart failure becomes short of breath when lying flat. Which position is MOST appropriate for treatment in bed?", ["Fowler's position", "Trendelenburg position", "Prone position", "Flat supine position"], "Fowler's position elevates the head and trunk, easing breathing for patients with orthopnea. Trendelenburg and flat positions increase venous return and can worsen dyspnea."],
        ["Which exercise moves primarily in the frontal plane?", ["Side-lying hip abduction", "Forward walking lunge", "Seated trunk rotation", "Standing hamstring curl"], "Hip abduction moves the limb away from midline in the frontal plane. Lunges and hamstring curls are sagittal, and trunk rotation is transverse."],
        ["During a pulse check, you palpate the dorsalis pedis artery. Where should your fingers be?", ["On the top of the foot", "On the sole of the foot", "Behind the medial ankle", "Behind the knee"], "Dorsal refers to the top of the foot, where the dorsalis pedis is palpated. Behind the medial malleolus is the posterior tibial pulse, and behind the knee is the popliteal."],
        ["A patient has pain in the right lower quadrant with fever and nausea. Which organ is MOST classically associated with this region?", ["Appendix", "Spleen", "Stomach", "Liver"], "The appendix lies in the right lower quadrant, and RLQ pain with fever and nausea is a classic appendicitis presentation needing urgent referral. The spleen and stomach are in the LUQ; the liver is in the RUQ."]
